{"AccessTokenContext validates grantType twice and never validates rawTokenId, so a null rawTokenId can slip through and later be encoded into the token id as ':null' or break downstream code expecting a non-null id": 0.9580497741699219, "AssertEvents.isAccessTokenId() uses the wrong substring indices and inverts the grant-shortcut equality check, so it rejects correct access-token IDs and can also throw StringIndexOutOfBoundsException for short prefixes": 0.998327910900116, "DefaultTokenContextEncoderProvider hard-codes a 6-character context (2+2+2), but OAuth2GrantTypeFactory.getShortcut() is documented as 'usually like 3-letters', and encoding does not validate shortcut length; a custom grant using a non-2-char shortcut will produce token IDs that later fail decoding": 0.9406933188438416, "StandardTokenExchangeProvider adds an import for TokenExchangeGrantTypeFactory but never uses it, which can fail builds in environments enforcing unused-import checks": 0.7428795695304871}